**Definition 4.4 (The scope of the support obstruction).** The failure
in (4.8) is failure of a cone representation, including its full TP
slice. Thus no whole-channel-preserving decomposition can replace
every feasible channel by boundary atoms. It does not state that an
optimizer needs full-sector atoms, that a boundary-supported channel
cannot attain $\varepsilon_1$, or that an objective-specific no-worse
map to a smaller class is impossible. Such a map would require a
separate proof for (1.3). The port (4.10) is a separation witness,
not a sufficient endpoint improvement near the QJM upper bound.

